---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PlaygroundShell from '../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Interactive Physics Atlas · Ganlin Xiang" description="Interactive mechanics, wave, electric-field, and electric-potential experiments built with native Canvas and TypeScript." active="playground" canonicalPath="/playground.html">
  <main id="content" class="main playground-page"><div class="container">
    <header class="playground-hero reveal"><div><span class="eyebrow">Interactive Physics Atlas / 001–EM 01</span><h1 class="page-title-text">Physics<br /><em>Atlas.</em></h1></div><div class="playground-intro"><p>Turn equations into experiments: launch a projectile, perturb a chaotic pendulum, paint wave interference, and probe electric fields from movable charges.</p><p class="formula-note">No pre-baked animation. Every vector, contour, trajectory, and readout comes from a numerical or analytic model with an explicit validity range.</p></div></header>
    <PlaygroundShell />
    <section class="playground-notes reveal" aria-labelledby="lab-notes-title"><span class="section-kicker">Lab notes</span><h2 id="lab-notes-title">What the instruments calculate</h2><div class="lab-note-grid"><article><span>01 / BALLISTICS</span><h3>Analytic trajectory</h3><p><code>x=v₀cos(θ)t</code><br /><code>y=v₀sin(θ)t−½gt²</code></p></article><article><span>02 / CHAOS</span><h3>Coupled nonlinear motion</h3><p>Two generalized angles are integrated with a fixed-step fourth-order Runge–Kutta method.</p></article><article><span>03 / INTERFERENCE</span><h3>Wave superposition</h3><p><code>u=Σ A sin(kr−ωt+φ)e<sup>−αr</sup></code></p></article><article><span>EM 01 / ELECTROSTATICS</span><h3>Field &amp; potential</h3><p><code>E=(1/4πε₀)Σqᵢ(r−rᵢ)/|r−rᵢ|³</code><br /><code>E=−∇V</code></p></article></div></section>
  </div></main>
  <script src="../scripts/playground/main.ts"></script>
</BaseLayout>
